# diff-wasm artifacts: GENERATED AST packs (via scripts/build-ast-packs.ts,
# rebuild with `npm run diff:build-wasm`) and cargo build trees. The text
# crate (text-build/) is NOT a scratch tree — it is the text-wasm's recipe
# and has no generator: it is TRACKED, so a fresh clone can rebuild.
# (Vestigial entries for the old packages/tooling/diff-wasm/* location and
# the deleted ast-build/ fork-copy are gone with them.)
/packages/framework/diff-wasm/ast/
/packages/framework/diff-wasm/target/
/packages/framework/diff-wasm/text-build/target/
/packages/framework/diff-wasm/src/natalia_diff_wasm.wasm
/packages/framework/object-store/native-index/target/
/packages/framework/object-store/native/target/
# The native-terminal package's PREBUILT drop directory: the one place a
# downloaded/unpacked Natalia (or a developer) drops the three terminal
# executables into (prebuilt/<triple>/). It holds multi-hundred-MB binaries,
# so it is never version-controlled — the resolver finds whatever a drop
# left there, and the archive/release stages its own copy.
/packages/plugins/native-terminal/prebuilt/
/packages/hosts/confinement/native/target/

# Local CEF SDK/test artifacts
.cef-test/
.cef-windows/
.cef-macos/
.cef-windows-download.tar.bz2
about-gpu-*.txt
*.bdic
apps/cef-desktop/build/

# Local Bun install cache (BUN_INSTALL override for sandboxed/read-only-home environments)
/.bun-local/

# NOT ignored: `/.nataliaignore` used to be listed here, which meant a fix to the
# checkpoint's ignore rules silently stayed local. That is exactly what happened:
# the measured `checkpoint incomplete (pre_tool)` fix (session scratch and
# minidumps blowing the 512MiB byte guard) was written into the file, the commit
# said "2 files changed", and the file itself was refused by git with
# "The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files".
# It is a product input — the capture reads it — so it is tracked.

# Downloaded build tools (the AppImage packer, ~9MB): never a repo artifact.
.tools/

# Scratch space for build logs, probes and one-off experiments (the repo's own
# working convention: /tmp dies between shell calls, this survives). Ignored so
# a stray draft cannot be committed, and so prettier's **/*.md glob does not
# fail the format gate on files that were never meant to ship.
.btmp/
/packages/plugins/native-terminal/native/pty-bridge/target/

# Machine-local runtime state: never tracked, never shipped
.natalia/

# Machine-local scratch. `.btmp/` is this repo's documented scratch root and is
# ignored; `.bttmp/` (two t's) is a node compile-cache directory that a broad
# `git add` swept into history on 2026-10-04 and cost two megabytes of binary
# cache in the tree. Ignore it by name so the same sweep cannot repeat.
.bttmp/
